  "term": "modafinil",
  "definition": "Modafinil is a synthetic central nervous system stimulant that promotes wakefulness. It appears to work in part by blocking dopamine reuptake, which raises dopamine levels outside nerve cells, and it may improve cognitive function in some clinical situations.",
